# The checks that ship-pr's `pr-review.sh checks` and `merge` treat as advisory on this
# repository's PRs, one ERE per line; a name any line matches is advisory. The lines replace the
# script's default list, so the first spells the default names in. The second matches exactly
# the two macOS jobs of skill-scripts.yml: the maintainer's decision is that a PR merges without
# waiting for the macOS runner queue, and those jobs still run on the merged tip, where `base`
# judges them (only the fleet-worker gate's `base --advisory-red` reads this file, to launch over
# a red that is only in jobs it names: ludics-lite#651).
# Read from the default branch: a PR's edit to this file applies only once that PR has merged.
# Re-check it when the workflow's job names change. No required job may `needs:` either macOS job
# (the boundary in SHIP_PR_ADVISORY_CHECKS's entry in pr-review.sh's usage text).
^(claude|Claude Code|github pages docs)$
^bash 3\.2 suites, .* \(macos\)$
